escaped space + glob:
[a b/*zz*]
[a b/x1][a b/x2]
[a b/?zz]
[a b/[q]zz]
[a b/x1]
[no pe*]
[a b/][a b/*zz*]
escaped space, no glob, and quoted forms (were right):
[a b/x1]
[a b/*zz*]
[a b/x1][a b/x2]
escaped space + brace, + a variable, in a for loop:
[a b][a c]
[a b/x1][a b/x2]
[a b/x1]
[a b/x2]
an IFS character in literal text:
[ab:c1]
[ab:c*]
a tilde whose home has a space:
[h o]
[h o/f1]
[h o/f1]
expansion results still split:
[p][q]
[a][b/x*]
